<!doctype html>
<html lang="{{ request.locale.iso_code }}" dir="{{ settings.text_direction }}">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta http-equiv="X-UA-Compatible" content="IE=edge">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <link rel="canonical" href="{{ canonical_url }}">
    {%- if settings.favicon != blank -%}
      <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="{{ settings.favicon | image_url: width: 32, height: 32 }}">
    {%- endif -%}

    <title>{{ page_title }}{% if current_tags %} &ndash; {{ current_tags | join: ', ' }}{% endif %}{% unless page_title contains shop.name %} &ndash; {{ shop.name }}{% endunless %}</title>
    {%- if page_description -%}<meta name="description" content="{{ page_description | escape }}">{%- endif -%}

    {% render 'meta-tags' %}

    {{ content_for_header }}

    {{ 'base.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
    {{ 'components.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
    {{ 'header-system.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
    {{ 'catalog-system.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
    {{ 'badges.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
    {{ 'home-mobile.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
    {{ 'cart.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
    {{ 'motion.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

    {%- comment -%}
      Every global token the merchant controls is written once here, so a colour
      change in the theme editor reaches every component without touching CSS.
      Section-level overrides are written onto the section root instead.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {% render 'theme-tokens' %}

    {%- comment -%}
      Arabic faces. Declared after the tokens so they can build on the
      merchant's chosen Latin family, and scoped by unicode-range so a shop
      running in French never downloads them.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {% render 'arabic-type' %}

    {%- comment -%}
      Direction, before first paint.

      Every other script here is deferred, which is right for behaviour and
      wrong for this: a returning Arabic reader would get a frame of the
      French layout, then a flip. This one runs where it stands, reads the
      shopper's stored choice and sets the attribute the whole stylesheet
      keys on. It is four lines and touches nothing else.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <script>
      (function () {
        try {
          var d = localStorage.getItem("souq:dir");
          if (d === "rtl" || d === "ltr") {
            document.documentElement.setAttribute("dir", d);
            document.documentElement.setAttribute("lang", d === "rtl" ? "ar" : "{{ request.locale.iso_code }}");
          }
        } catch (e) {}
      })();
    </script>

    <script src="{{ 'theme.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>
  </head>

  <body class="template-{{ request.page_type | handle }}">
    <a class="skip-to-content visually-hidden" href="#MainContent">
      {{ 'accessibility.skip_to_content' | t }}
    </a>

    {% sections 'header-group' %}

    <main id="MainContent" tabindex="-1" role="main">
      {{ content_for_layout }}
    </main>

    {% sections 'footer-group' %}

    {%- comment -%}
      The cart drawer lives outside every section so one instance serves the
      whole site: add from a card on the homepage, from the product page, or
      from a collection, and the same drawer opens.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {% render 'cart-drawer' %}

    {%- comment -%}
      Toast target. theme.js has always had a toast() for add-to-cart, and the
      element it looks for was never in any layout — so every confirmation it
      tried to show went nowhere. Polite, not assertive: it reports something
      the shopper just did rather than interrupting what they are reading.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="toast" data-toast data-open="false" role="status" aria-live="polite">
      <span class="toast__icon" aria-hidden="true">{% render 'icon', name: 'badge-check' %}</span>
      <span data-toast-text></span>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
